[center][color=#58D1B2][size=5][b]Font Choices[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]Optional, language-aware font profiles for Fields of Mistria.[/color][/center]

[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]About[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]Font Choices adds an optional Settings category for supported game languages. Pick a reviewed font profile for all text, or keep the game's original font. It does not add, replace, or translate languages.[/color]

[color=#F3EEE7]The mod changes only the currently selected language when that language has an explicitly supported profile. Unknown and future languages are left untouched.[/color]

[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Features[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Language-aware font choices, with profiles limited to languages whose glyph coverage has been checked.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Separate choices for all text, standard UI, popup descriptions, and dialogue text where a reviewed combination supports them.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]A global Experimental picker for opt-in font and metric comparisons across all text roles.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Safe saved-setting handling: an unavailable selection falls back to a normal available profile or the game's original font.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]No game localization files are replaced or edited.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Experimental profiles[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]Experimental profiles are intentionally opt-in. They are useful for trying a font family and its metric profile in the actual game UI, but some combinations can be less readable or take more room than curated choices. The picker applies one selection to all text roles at once, so the active result is always unambiguous.[/color]

[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Supported languages[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]Available choices depend on the selected game language. Current profiles cover Bulgarian, English, French, Spanish, Portuguese, Polish, Russian, and Turkish. A language is shown only when its profile has been deliberately configured; this avoids applying an unsuitable font to text the mod has not reviewed.[/color]

[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Install a current version of Mistria Modding API / your compatible mod manager, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/949]AIM[/url] or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/78]MOMI [/url].[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Install Font Choices.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Start the game, then open Settings and select Font Choices (it has different name on every supported language).[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]Font Choices is an independent UI add-on. It does not overwrite translation packages and does not modify game files. Font rendering and UI layout can still vary by language, font, and game version, so please report any font/language combination that is hard to read or clips in an interface.[/color]

[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Included font licenses[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]Each distributed font is accompanied by its applicable license text inside the mod package.[/color]
